addrmap hi3518av100 {
    name = "hi3518av100 registers";
    desc = "
        ## Datasheets

        * [Full Datasheet](assets/Hi3518-Datasheet.pdf)
        * [User Guide](assets/Hi3518-UserGuide.pdf)

        ## Diagrams

        ![Logic Block Diagram](assets/Hi3518AV100-Logic-Block-Diagram.png)

        <!-- overview:begin -->

        ### Diagrams

        ![Logic block diagram](assets/diagrams/hi3518av100-logic.svg)

        ![Register blocks by function](assets/diagrams/hi3518av100-blocks.svg)

        ![Clock tree](assets/diagrams/hi3518av100-clocks.svg)

        ![Boot flow](assets/diagrams/hi3518av100-boot.svg)

        ![Video pipeline](assets/diagrams/hi3518av100-video.svg)

        ![Interrupt topology](assets/diagrams/hi3518av100-irq.svg)

        ![Reset tree](assets/diagrams/hi3518av100-resets.svg)

        ![Storage, USB and Ethernet paths](assets/diagrams/hi3518av100-io.svg)

        ![DMA request lines](assets/diagrams/hi3518av100-dma.svg)

        ![Bus masters and DDR QoS groups](assets/diagrams/hi3518av100-busqos.svg)

        ![Power domains](assets/diagrams/hi3518av100-power.svg)

        ![CRG register map](assets/diagrams/hi3518av100-crgmap.svg)

        ![IP editions across the camera family](assets/diagrams/hi3518av100-editions.svg)

        ### Camera family comparison (data sheet chapter 1)

        One column per chip, taken from the data sheets named in the header row below; `-` = the sheet gives no value. The Hi3518 sheet covers the A and C variants; the Hi3518E V200 sheet covers V200, V201 and Hi3516C V200.

        | Item | Hi3516 V100 | Hi3516C V100 | Hi3518A V100 | Hi3518C V100 | Hi3518E V100 | Hi3516C V300 | Hi3516E V100 | Hi3518E V200 | Hi3518E V201 | Hi3516C V200 |
        |---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
        | Data sheet (issue, date, language) | 00B60 2011-08-12, Chinese | 00B02 2013-02-05 | Hi3518 sheet (A and C in one document) | same document as A | 03 2015-11-26 | 05 2018-05-10 (C V300 and E V100 in one document) | same document as C V300 | 02 2017-06-12 (one document for V200, V201, Hi3516C V200) | same document | same document |
        | CPU | Cortex-A9 up to 800 MHz, VFP, 32 KB I + 32 KB D L1, 256 KB L2, about 2000 DMIPS | ARM926 up to 440 MHz, 16 KB I + 16 KB D, 2 KB ITCM | ARM926 up to 440 MHz, 16 KB I + 16 KB D, 2 KB ITCM | ARM926 up to 440 MHz, 16 KB I + 16 KB D, 2 KB ITCM | ARM926 up to 440 MHz, 16 KB I + 16 KB D | ARM926 up to 800 MHz, 32 KB I + 32 KB D | ARM926 up to 800 MHz, 32 KB I + 32 KB D | ARM926 540 MHz, 32 KB I + 32 KB D | ARM926 540 MHz, 32 KB I + 32 KB D | ARM926 600 MHz, 32 KB I + 32 KB D |
        | Interrupt controller | ARM GIC (A9 MPCore), IDs 0-31 internal | PL190 VIC | PL190 VIC | PL190 VIC | PL190 VIC | PL190 VIC | PL190 VIC | PL190 VIC | PL190 VIC | PL190 VIC |
        | DDR | DDR2/DDR3, 32 or 16 bit, up to 500 MHz, 1 GB (32 bit) / 512 MB (16 bit) | DDR2/DDR3, 16 bit, up to 440 MHz, up to 256 MB | DDR2/DDR3, 16 bit, up to 400 MHz, up to 256 MB | DDR2/DDR3, 16 bit, up to 400 MHz, up to 128 MB | embedded 16-bit DDR2, up to 512 Mbit | external 16-bit DDR3/DDR3L, up to 4 Gbit | embedded 512 Mbit DDR (1.8 V) | embedded 16-bit DDR2 512 Mbit, 360 MHz | embedded 16-bit DDR2 256 Mbit, 360 MHz | external 16-bit DDR2/DDR3/DDR3L, up to 4 Gbit, 400 MHz |
        | Boot media | NAND, SPI flash, or PCIe load into DDR | SPI NOR, NAND | SPI NOR, NAND | SPI NOR only | SPI NOR only | SPI NOR/NAND, eMMC (4-bit), serial (fastboot), SD/USB update | same as C V300 (SPI NOR/NAND, eMMC, fastboot, update) | serial (BOOTROM), SPI NOR/NAND, eMMC | same as V200 | same as V200 |
        | Flash controllers | NANDC (2 CS), SFC (2 CS) | SFC (1 CS), NANDC | SFC (1 CS), NANDC | SFC (1 CS) | SFC (1 CS) | FMC (SPI NOR/NAND), eMMC via MMC | FMC, eMMC via MMC | FMC, eMMC | FMC, eMMC | FMC, eMMC |
        | Video encoder | H.264 BP/MP/HP, MPEG4 SP, JPEG; up to 16 Mpixel | H.264 BP/MP, MJPEG/JPEG; 1080p@30 + VGA@30 + JPEG 1080p@1 | H.264 BP/MP, MJPEG/JPEG; 720p@30 + VGA@30 + QVGA@30 + JPEG 720p@1 | H.264 BP/MP, MJPEG/JPEG; 720p@30 + QVGA@30 + JPEG 720p@1 | H.264 BP/MP, MJPEG/JPEG; 720p@25 + JPEG 720p@3 | H.264 BP/MP/HP, H.265 Main, MJPEG/JPEG; 2048x2048@15 + 640x640@15, or 1080p@30 + 480p@30 + 240p@30 | same codecs; 1536x1536 (width up to 2048); 1080p@20 + 576p@20 | H.264 BP/MP/HP, MJPEG/JPEG; 1080p@20 | H.264 BP/MP/HP, MJPEG/JPEG; 960p@25 (no LDC, no 90/270 rotation) | H.264 BP/MP/HP, MJPEG/JPEG; 1080p@30 |
        | Video in | 8-16 bit RGB Bayer up to 150 MHz, BT.601/656/1120, dual sensor | 8/10/12-bit Bayer up to 74.25 MHz, BT.656/BT.1120 | 8/10/12-bit Bayer up to 74.25 MHz, BT.656/BT.1120 | 8/10/12-bit Bayer up to 74.25 MHz, BT.656/BT.1120 | 8/10/12-bit Bayer up to 74.25 MHz, BT.656/BT.1120, 1080p@30 / 720p@30 | 8-14 bit Bayer DC, BT.601/656/1120, MIPI, LVDS/sub-LVDS, HiSPi, up to 2048x2048 and 250 Mpixel/s | same as C V300 | MIPI / LVDS / HiSPi / BT.656 (VICAP) | same as V200 | same as V200, plus differential and single-ended pin modes |
        | Video out | CVBS, BT.656, BT.1120 (1080p@30) | CVBS, BT.1120 (1080p@30) | CVBS, BT.1120 | BT.1120 (no CVBS) | BT.1120 (no CVBS) | PAL/NTSC CVBS, BT.656, 6-bit RGB565 LCD | BT.656, RGB565 LCD (no CVBS) | - | - | - |
        | Ethernet | GMAC 10/100/1000, RGMII/MII | MAC 10/100, RGMII/MII | MAC 10/100, RGMII/MII | MAC 10/100, RGMII/MII | MAC 10/100, RMII/MII | MAC 10/100 RMII, TSO | MAC 10/100 RMII, TSO | MAC + internal FE PHY | MAC + internal FE PHY | MAC + internal FE PHY |
        | USB | 2 x USB 2.0 host | 1 x USB 2.0 host | 1 x USB 2.0 host | 1 x USB 2.0 host | 1 x USB 2.0 host | 1 x USB 2.0 host/device | 1 x USB 2.0 host/device | USB 2.0 host/device | USB 2.0 host/device | USB 2.0 host/device |
        | SDIO/MMC | 2 x MMC (SD/SDIO/eMMC) | 1 x SDIO 2.0 | 1 x SDIO 2.0 | 1 x SDIO 2.0 | 1 x SDIO 2.0 | 3 x SDIO 2.0 (two with 3.3/1.8 V) + eMMC 4.5 | 3 x SDIO 2.0 + eMMC 4.5 | 2 x SDIO + eMMC | 2 x SDIO + eMMC | 2 x SDIO + eMMC |
        | Package | FC-CSP 416, 15x15 mm, 0.65 mm | FCBGA 293, 13x13x1.37 mm, 0.65 mm | FCBGA 293, 13x13x1.37 mm, 0.65 mm | ePad QFP, 20x20x1.0 mm, 0.4 mm | BGA 220, 11x11 mm, 0.65 mm | TFBGA 273, 12x12 mm, 0.65 mm | TFBGA 231, 10x14 mm, 0.65 mm | TFBGA 192, 10x10 mm | TFBGA 192, 10x10 mm | TFBGA 273, 12x12 mm |
        | Typical power | 1200 mW | 850 mW | 700 mW | 700 mW (one value for the Hi3518 sheet) | 900 mW | 550 mW (1080p30) | 600 mW (1080p20) | - | - | - |
        | Core / DDR voltage | 1.0 V core; 1.8/1.5 V DDR; 2.5 V, 3.3 V | 1.2 V; 1.5/1.8 V DDR; 3.3 V I/O | 1.2 V; 1.5/1.8 V DDR; 3.3 V I/O | 1.2 V; 1.5/1.8 V DDR; 3.3 V I/O | 1.2 V; 1.8 V embedded DDR; 3.3 V I/O | 0.9 V; 1.5/1.35 V DDR; 3.3 V I/O | 0.9 V; 1.8 V DDR; 3.3 V I/O | - | - | - |
        | Chip ID (SC_SYSID) | 0x3516_0100 | 0x3518_0100 (as printed in the sheet) | 0x3518_0100 | 0x3518_0100 | 0x3518_0100 (as printed) | 0x3516_C300 | 0x3516_C300 (one value printed for both) | 0x3518E200, SCSYSID0[31:24] = 0x02 | 0x3518E200, [31:24] = 0x03 | 0x3518E200, [31:24] = 0x01 |
        | SDK kernel | - | Linux 3.0.y | Linux 3.0.y | Linux 3.0.y | Linux 3.0.y | Linux 3.18 | Linux 3.18 | - | - | - |

        Differences the data sheets state: the Hi3518C has no NAND controller, no CVBS output, no 90/270 degree rotation, no autofocus, two UARTs, no SSP/IR and 128 MB maximum DDR; the Hi3516C V100 is the Hi3518A with 1080p encoding; the Hi3518E V100 is a 720p part with embedded DDR2 and no NAND controller; the Hi3516E V100 differs from the Hi3516C V300 by embedded 512 Mbit DDR, a 231-pin package, no CVBS output, no two-frame WDR and the lower encoder limit; the Hi3518E V200/V201/Hi3516C V200 differ in CPU speed, DDR, package and encoder performance (table in the root description above).

        Chip: Hi3518A V100 (Hi3518 HD IP Camera SoC data sheet (Hi3518A and Hi3518C), chapter 1).

        ### Boot selection (data sheet 1.3 / 1.4)

        | Strap | Boot medium |
        |---|---|
        | BOOT_SEL (MDCK) = 0 | SPI NOR flash (SFC) |
        | BOOT_SEL (MDCK) = 1 | NAND flash (NANDC), Hi3518A only |

        NAND boot also latches NF_BOOT_PIN0..4 (shared with NF_REN, NF_CLE, NF_ALE, NF_WEN pins) at power-on to select page size, ECC type, block size and address cycles; SFC_ADDR_MODE (shared with SFC_CLK) selects the default SPI NOR address mode (0 = 3-byte, 1 = 4-byte); both are readable in SYS_CTRL SYSSTAT (sfc_addr_mode, nf_ecc_type).

        ### Memory map notes

        * Same map as the Hi3516C V100: 0x00000000 remap window (boot space chosen by BOOT_SEL, TCM after remap clear), NAND space 0x50000000 (Hi3518A only, reserved on the Hi3518C), SPI flash 0x58000000, DDR 0x80000000 window 256 MB (Table 1-1).

        ### DMA request lines (data sheet Table 3-24 (3-23 on the Hi3518E V100), DMAC at 0x100D0000)

        | Req | Peripheral | Req | Peripheral | Req | Peripheral | Req | Peripheral |
        |---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
        | 0 | SIO receive (RX) | 4 | Reserved | 8 | UART1 RX | 12 | SSP1 RX |
        | 1 | SIO transmit (TX) | 5 | Reserved | 9 | UART1 TX | 13 | SSP1 TX |
        | 2 | Reserved | 6 | UART0 RX | 10 | UART2 RX | 14 | SSP0 RX |
        | 3 | Reserved | 7 | UART0 TX | 11 | UART2 TX | 15 | SSP0 TX |

        On the Hi3518C the SSP request lines 12-15 are reserved (the sheet marks them). Channel 0 has the highest priority and channel 3 the lowest; memory-to-memory transfers should use channel 2 or 3 (the DMAC inserts an idle cycle after each bus operation on those channels).

        ### Pin multiplexing summary (generated from the IO_CONFIG registers)

        95 one-per-pin `muxctrl_regN` registers. Alternate functions per interface, as named in the register enumerations (GPIO is always one of the choices); 0 pins have no alternate function other than GPIO. Per-pin choices are in the IO_CONFIG register pages.

        | Interface | Functions |
        |---|---|
        | Serial flash (SFC / FMC) | SFC_ADDR_MODE, SFC_CLK, SFC_DIO, SFC_DOI, SFC_HOLD_IO3, SFC_WP_IO2 |
        | NAND (NANDC) | NF_ALE, NF_BOOT_PIN0-3, NF_CLE, NF_CSN0, NF_CSN1, NF_DQ0-7, NF_RDY0, NF_RDY1, NF_REN, NF_WEN |
        | SD / SDIO / eMMC | SDIO_CARD_DETECT, SDIO_CARD_POWER, SDIO_CCLK_OUT, SDIO_CCMD, SDIO_CDATA0-3, SDIO_CWPR |
        | Ethernet (MAC, MII/RMII/RGMII, MDIO, PHY clock) | EPHY_CLK, MDCK, MDIO, MII_COL, MII_CRS, MII_RXCK, MII_RXD0-3, MII_RXDV, MII_RXER, MII_TXCK, MII_TXD0-3, MII_TXEN, MII_TXER, RMII_CLK |
        | Video input (VI / VIU) | VIU_CLK, VIU_DAT0-11, VIU_HS, VIU_VS |
        | Video output (VO / LCD) | VOU1120_CLK, VOU1120_DATA0-15 |
        | Sensor control | FLASH_TRIG, SENSOR_CLK, SHUTTER_TRIG |
        | UART | UART1_CTSN, UART1_RTSN, UART1_RXD, UART1_TXD, UART2_RXD, UART2_TXD |
        | SPI / SSP | SPI0_SCLK, SPI0_SDI, SPI0_SDO, SPI1_CSN, SPI1_SCLK, SPI1_SDI, SPI1_SDO |
        | I2C | I2C_SCL, I2C_SDA |
        | PWM | PWM_OUT0, PWM_OUT1 |
        | IR, ADC, USB, JTAG | IR, JTAG_TCK, JTAG_TDI, JTAG_TDO, JTAG_TMS, JTAG_TRSTN, USB_OVRCUR, USB_PWREN |
        | Boot straps and test | BOOT_SEL, CLK_TEST_OUT0-3 |
        | Other | PLL_TEST_OUT0-3, RTC_TEST_CLK, SVB_PWM, SYS_RSTN_OUT, TEMPER_DQ |

        ### Clocks (data sheet 3.2, Tables 3-2 and 3-3)

        Inputs: XIN (24 MHz crystal, PLL input only), RTC_XIN (32 kHz), VIU_CLK (video input clock), MII_RXCK / MII_TXCK (ETH). Four PLLs, two configuration registers each: APLL PERI_CRG0/1, VPLL0 PERI_CRG2/3, BPLL PERI_CRG4/5, EPLL PERI_CRG8/9 (the Hi3518E V100 sheet names the DDR clock row BPLL in its Table 3-3).

        | PLL output | Default | Feeds |
        |---|---|---|
        | APLL FOUTPOSTDIV | 440 MHz | ARM9 clock |
        | second POSTDIV row (printed as APLL; BPLL in the Hi3518E V100 sheet and Table 3-2: INFERRED) | 440 MHz | DDR clock; AXI = DDR / 2, APB = DDR / 4 |
        | VPLL0 FOUTVCO | 1188 MHz | /6 = 198 MHz VPSS and TDE; /12 = 99 MHz MDU, NFC, CIPHER (MDU and CIPHER on the Hi3518E V100) |
        | VPLL0 FOUT2 | 74.25 MHz | VDP HD |
        | EPLL FOUTVCO | 1350 MHz | /2 = 675 MHz SIO MCLK source; /6 = 225 MHz VEDU, JPGE, VAPU; /12 = 112.5 MHz SFC; 54 MHz VDP SD; 27 MHz sensor clock |

        Timer count clocks: SC_CTRL timeren0ov/1ov/2ov/3ov (bits 16, 18, 20, 22) select the reference clock (0) or the bus clock (1) for each timer pair counter. Per-IP dividers/selects and clock gates are in the CRG register pages (the gate map above).

        ### Reset and power

        * Reset sources (data sheet 3.1): the RSTN pin or the internal POR module, selected by the POR_SEL pin (RSTN low for longer than 12 XIN cycles with XIN running); the global soft reset from the system controller (sys_rst_req, deasserts after at least 360 system clocks, does not reset the CRG and test circuits); per-module soft resets xx_srst_req from the CRG (set 1 to reset, written back to 0 to release, never self-clearing).
        * Low-power: two system modes, normal and standby (slow/doze); clock gating per module, module low-power control, DDR self-refresh (DDRC_SREFCTRL); no power-domain switching is described. Typical power is 700-900 mW.

        ### Bus ports (system controller registers)

        | Bus | Masters | Slaves |
        |---|---|---|
        | SYS AXI | AHB bridge (port0), ARMD (CPU data) (port1), IVE (port2), ARMI (CPU instruction) (port3) | s1 AHB (peripheral bridge), s2 APB_SYS, s3 APB_MEDIA, s4 MDDRC (DDR controller) |
        | media AXI | VENC (port0), VPSS (port1), TDE (port2), JPGE (port3), MDU (port4) | (towards DDR) |

        Source: PERIPHCTRL5-13 (timeout, priority registers of the system bus and the media bus); priority 7 = highest on the media bus, 4 = highest on the system bus; timeout count = value x 2. The data sheets name only the bus master ports of the registers; which peripheral sits behind each AHB master port is not stated (the SYS AXI masters are arbitrated at the MDDRC slave port s4).

        ### Interrupts (ARM926 VIC source numbers, data sheet Table 3-21)

        | # | Source | # | Source | # | Source |
        |---|---|---|---|---|---|
        | 0 | Global software interrupt | 11 | SFC | 22 | VICAP |
        | 1 | WDT interrupt when periphctrl0 bit[31] is 0 | 12 | ETH | 23 | VOU |
        | 2 | RTC interrupt when periphctrl0 bit[31] is 0 | 13 | CIPHER | 24 | VEDU |
        | 3 | Timer0/Timer1 | 14 | DMAC | 25 | UART2 |
        | 4 | Timer2/Timer3 | 15 | USB_EHCI | 26 | JPGE |
        | 5 | UART0/UART1 | 16 | USB_OHCI | 27 | TDE |
        | 6 | SSP0 | 17 | VPSS | 28 | MDU/DDRT |
        | 7 | SSP1 | 18 | SDIO | 29 | GPIO0/GPIO1/GPIO2/GPIO11 |
        | 8 | NANDC | 19 | IR/SAR_ADC | 30 | GPIO3/GPIO4/GPIO5/GPIO10 |
        | 9 | SIO | 20 | I2C | 31 | GPIO6/GPIO7/GPIO8/GPIO9 |
        | 10 | Temper_Cap | 21 | IVE |  |  |

        ### Clock-gate and reset map (generated from the CRG registers)

        | Offset | Register | Description | Gate / reset fields |
        |---|---|---|---|
        | 0x028 | PERI_CRG10 | ARM9/DDR frequency mode and reset configuration register | cpu_srst_req |
        | 0x02C | PERI_CRG11 | VICAP clock and reset configuration register | vi_hrst_req, vi1_hcken, vi_rst_req, vi_cken, isp_rst_req, isp_cken |
        | 0x034 | PERI_CRG13 | VOU clock and reset control register | vo_hrst_req, vo_hd_srst_req, vo_sd_srst_req, vou_hcken, vou_hd_cken, vou_sd_cken |
        | 0x038 | PERI_CRG14 | PWM clock and reset control register | pwm_srst_req, pwm_cken |
        | 0x040 | PERI_CRG16 | VEDU clock and soft reset control register | vedu_srst_req, vedu0_cken |
        | 0x048 | PERI_CRG18 | VPSS clock and reset control register | vps_srst_req, vps_cken |
        | 0x058 | PERI_CRG22 | TDE clock and soft reset control register | tde_srst_req, tde_cken |
        | 0x060 | PERI_CRG24 | JPGE clock and soft reset control register | jpge_srst_req, jpge_cken |
        | 0x068 | PERI_CRG26 | MDU clock and soft reset control register | mdu_srst_req, mdu_cken |
        | 0x06C | PERI_CRG27 | VAPU clock and soft reset control register | vapu_srst_req, vapu_cken |
        | 0x07C | PERI_CRG31 | CIPHER clock and soft reset control register | cipher_srst_req, cipher_cken |
        | 0x080 | PERI_CRG32 | SAR ADC control register | sar_adc_srst_req, sar_adc_cken |
        | 0x08C | PERI_CRG35 | SIO clock and soft reset control register | sio_srst_req, sio_cken, adac_srst_req |
        | 0x0B8 | PERI_CRG46 | USB clock and soft reset control register | usb_ahb_srst_req, usb_cken |
        | 0x0C0 | PERI_CRG48 | SFC clock and soft reset control register | sfc_srst_req, sfc_cken |
        | 0x0C4 | PERI_CRG49 | SDIO clock and soft reset control register | sdio_srst_req, sdio_cken |
        | 0x0CC | PERI_CRG51 | ETH interface clock and soft reset control register | hrst_eth_s, eth_cken |
        | 0x0D0 | PERI_CRG52 | NANDC clock and soft reset control register | nfc_srst_req, nfc_cken |
        | 0x0D8 | PERI_CRG54 | DDRTEST clock and soft reset control register | efuse_srst_req, efuse_cken, ddrtest_srst_req, ddrtest_cken |
        | 0x0E0 | PERI_CRG56 | DMA clock and soft reset control register | dma_srst_req, dma_cken |
        | 0x0E4 | PERI_CRG57 | Soft reset control register for other CRG interface modules | test_clk_en, i2c_srst_req, t_cap_srst_req, ir_srst_req, ssp0_srst_req, ssp1_srst_req, uart0_srst_req, uart1_srst_req, uart2_srst_req, ir_cken, ... |
        | 0x0F4 | PERI_CRG61 | Speed monitor control register | osc_clk_en, osc_en |

        Only fields whose names contain a clock-enable or reset keyword are listed; the field descriptions in the register pages give the polarity and the clocks they gate.

        ### Register blocks (generated from this description)

        | Base | Instance | Block | Register space |
        |---|---|---|---|
        | 0x10000000 | NANDC | HiSilicon parallel NAND flash controller (hinfc300/301/504 family) | 156 B |
        | 0x10010000 | SFC | System Flash Controller Registers | 1088 B |
        | 0x10020000 | SDIO | HiSilicon MMC/SD/SDIO controller (DesignWare-MMC based, himciv200) | 260 B |
        | 0x10090000 | ETH | HiSilicon femac v2 Fast Ethernet MAC with MDIO | 5184 B |
        | 0x100A0000 | OHCI | HiSilicon USB 2.0 host controller - OHCI | 92 B |
        | 0x100B0000 | EHCI | HiSilicon USB 2.0 host controller - EHCI | 176 B |
        | 0x100C0000 | CIPHER | CIPHER (8 channels) | 5184 B |
        | 0x100D0000 | DMAC | HiSilicon DMA controller (PL080-compatible, 4 or 8 channels) | 384 B |
        | 0x10140000 | VIC | Vectored interrupt controller (ARM PrimeCell PL190) | 4 KB |
        | 0x20000000 | TIMER0 | Timer Registers | 28 B |
        | 0x20000020 | TIMER1 | Timer Registers | 28 B |
        | 0x20010000 | TIMER2 | Timer Registers | 28 B |
        | 0x20010020 | TIMER3 | Timer Registers | 28 B |
        | 0x20030000 | CRG | Clock and reset generator (CRG), Hi3518A V100 / Hi3518C V100 | 252 B |
        | 0x20040000 | WDG | Watchdog Registers | 3076 B |
        | 0x20050000 | SYS_CTRL | System Controller Registers | 3824 B |
        | 0x20060000 | RTC | HiSilicon SPI-bridged RTC (APB registers) | 164 B |
        | 0x20070000 | IR | HiSilicon IR receiver | 56 B |
        | 0x20080000 | UART0 | UART (ARM PrimeCell PL011) | 4 KB |
        | 0x20090000 | UART1 | UART (ARM PrimeCell PL011) | 4 KB |
        | 0x200A0000 | UART2 | UART (ARM PrimeCell PL011) | 4 KB |
        | 0x200B0000 | SAR_ADC | HiSilicon SAR ADC (10-bit, 2 channels, first generation) | 32 B |
        | 0x200C0000 | SPI0 | SPI Registers | 48 B |
        | 0x200D0000 | I2C | HiSilicon I2C Master Controller | 32 B |
        | 0x200E0000 | SPI1 | SPI Registers | 48 B |
        | 0x200F0000 | IO_CONFIG | IO configuration (pin multiplexing), Hi3518A V100 | 380 B |
        | 0x20110000 | DDRC | DDRC Registers | 656 B |
        | 0x20120000 | DDR_PHY | DDR PHY (Synopsys DWC DDR PHY PUB) registers | 1600 B |
        | 0x20130000 | PWM | HiSilicon PWM group | 96 B |
        | 0x20140000 | GPIO0 | ARM PL061 | 1053 B |
        | 0x20150000 | GPIO1 | ARM PL061 | 1053 B |
